CONCLUSION

The organisational hierarchy was successfully represented using a general tree structure. Level-order traversal was used to display the hierarchy level by level.

Linear Search and Binary Search were implemented to locate department names. Linear Search can work with unsorted data, while Binary Search requires the department names to be sorted.

For the given department list, Binary Search generally requires fewer comparisons than Linear Search for the tested searches. Therefore, the tree representation is suitable for organisational reporting, while a sorted department list with Binary Search is suitable for efficient department searching.
